          "distinct": true,
          "id": "eab1e4316d9dc4d1ab8f9616fa4d0071a33e73fc",
          "message": "fix(firmware)!: read the device id from the base MAC (#191)\n\nOn chips with 802.15.4 (C6, H2, C5), esp_efuse_mac_get_default() returns\nan 8-byte EUI-64, not a 6-byte MAC. The old code read it into a 6-byte\nbuffer. That overflowed the buffer and kept the wrong bytes: the OUI\nplus the EUI-64 FF:FE padding (54:32:04:FF:FE:22) instead of the chip's\nreal MAC (54:32:04:22:7B:D4). The id was not unique and did not match\nthe USB serial or the id the host computes from it.\n\nesp_read_mac(ESP_MAC_BASE) returns the real 48-bit base MAC on every\nchip.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: the device id changes on 802.15.4 chips (C6, H2, C5,\nC61, H21, H4), from the old wrong value to the correct base-MAC id.\nAnything stored against the old id (device aliases, the device cache,\ndeploy or console targeting by id, on-device kv) needs to be set again\nafter updating firmware. Other chips (ESP32, S2, S3, C2, C3) are\nunchanged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-31T19:22:04.204Z",
          "tree_id": "",
