          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a646607b86785a1f3d09c650f1dc5188bc308ced",
          "message": "fix(releaser): derive changelog range from version bump commit (#263)\n\nrelease.yml pushes the release tag only after a successful publish, minutes after the release PR merges. A push landing in that window regenerated the rolling PR against the previous tag, re-listing commits that had already shipped. The base for changelogs and bump recommendations is now the commit that set package.json to its current version (the release-PR merge), so regeneration is correct at any moment and tags are no longer meaningful for range computation. The bump recommendation is computed from the same range (breaking: major, feat: minor, else patch), replacing the tag-dependent conventional-recommended-bump. Plan also skips when nothing landed since the last release, so a manual dispatch after a quiet release can't produce an empty patch-bump PR.",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-18T15:01:13.269Z",
