          "id": "a8dfe5cbcd65d7e6d8f52494e2154dbadb7e30a7",
          "message": "feat(cli)!: key heap snapshots by chip and tolerate small drift (#347)\n\n- Moves heap easurements to the `__heap_snapshots__` directory, one committed file per chip, keyed by test path.\n\n- Adds `mikro profile`, which reads the memory a device leaves for an app: the JS budget before `mem_limit` throws and the free system heap, reported in the ready handshake and captured before the app was evaluated.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: `--update-heap-baselines` is now `-u`, `--update-heap`. Committed `<name>.test.heap-baseline.json` files are no longer read; move their values into `__heap_snapshots__/<chip>.json` or let the next run record them again.",
